# The coefficients of the product of two polynomials of 2-limb coefficients (milestone2.md, "sum,
# dot, axpy, convolution": conv_k; "The product of polynomials"): x of n_x coefficients and y of
# n_y, z of n_x + n_y - 1 (none when a polynomial is empty). Coefficient j is the dot product dot_2,
# in its sequential order, of the terms (x_i, y_(j-i)), i from max(0, j - n_y + 1) to
# min(j, n_x - 1) in increasing order: if every coefficient is canonical, each coefficient that is
# finite satisfies the statement of dot_2 for its own m_j terms, m_j <= min(n_x, n_y), so that the
# exported bound of dot for min(n_x, n_y) terms covers every one. Its arrays are stored, written
# through Kairn (the centers of bv_conv_2): kairn::conv of two limbs calls conv_2_entry, whose
# coefficients guard the limbs of their terms (rule R3, the factors of a fused operation). A
# convolution (architecture.md, "Convolutions"): the mask finite is the and of the tests of the
# coefficients, and when it is false a second pass makes every coefficient that is not finite the
# canonical NaN ("When something is not finite"). The array written overlaps neither x nor y.
fold:          conv_2
arrays:        stored x = x0 x1, stored y = y0 y1
coefficients:  dot_2
state:         mask finite
combine:       finite = and(finite, finite)
orders:        sequential
writes:        z = z0 z1
check:         fold_finish_2
finish:        none
value:         x*y
requires:      canonical x
requires:      canonical y
ensures:       coefficients z
ensures:       finite_or_nan z flag=finite
min_precision: 4
theorem:       proofs/theories/FoldConv.v
ieee_theorem:  proofs/theories/IeeeFoldConv.v
terms_theorem: proofs/theories/FoldConv.v
status:        proved
domain:        extended
source:        dot_2 on the terms of each coefficient: Higham's bound for summation over any tree, through dot_2
license:       bound: published; proof: MIT
